{"name":"Heavy Hammock","hex":"#beb9a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heavy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having great weight.","Heavyset: overweight."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In a heavy manner; weightily; heavily; gravely.","To a great degree; greatly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heavy"},{"term":"hammock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A swinging couch or bed, usually made of netting or canvas about six feet (1.8 meters) wide, suspended by clews or cords at the ends.","A piece of land thickly wooded, and usually covered with bushes and vines."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lie in a hammock.","To hang in a way that resembles a hammock."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hammock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hammock","blocks":[{"text":"A hammock, from Spanish hamaca, borrowed from Taíno and Arawak hamaka, is a sling made of fabric, rope, or netting, suspended between two or more points, used for swinging, sleeping, or resting. It normally consists of one or more cloth panels, or a woven network of twine or thin rope stretched with ropes between two firm anchor points such as trees or posts. Hammocks were developed by native inhabitants of the Americas for sleeping, as well as the English. Later, they were used aboard ships by sailors to enable comfort and maximize available space, by explorers or soldiers travelling in wooded regions and eventually by parents in the early 1920s for containing babies just learning to crawl. Today they are popular around the world for relaxation; they are also used as a lightweight bed on camping trips. The hammock is often seen as a symbol of summer, leisure, relaxation and simple, easy living."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Hammock11.jpg/330px-Hammock11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammock","wikidata":"Q193823"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Hammock_%283711967150%29.jpg/500px-Hammock_%283711967150%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Hammock_%283711967150%29.jpg/500px-Hammock_%283711967150%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hammock beside the beach","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHammock_(3711967150).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Hexateuch%2C_Cotton_MS_Claudius_B_IV%2C_f._60r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png/500px-Hexateuch%2C_Cotton_MS_Claudius_B_IV%2C_f._60r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Hexateuch%2C_Cotton_MS_Claudius_B_IV%2C_f._60r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png/1280px-Hexateuch%2C_Cotton_MS_Claudius_B_IV%2C_f._60r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Hexateuch%2C_Cotton_MS_Claudius_B_IV%2C_f._60r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png/500px-Hexateuch%2C_Cotton_MS_Claudius_B_IV%2C_f._60r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joseph in a hammock on wheels (Hexateuch, 11th century)[6]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHexateuch%2C_Cotton_MS_Claudius_B_IV%2C_f._60r_(Ausschnitt_01).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Luttrell_Psalter%2C_Add_MS_42130%2C_f._200r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png/500px-Luttrell_Psalter%2C_Add_MS_42130%2C_f._200r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Luttrell_Psalter%2C_Add_MS_42130%2C_f._200r_%28Ausschnitt_01%29.png/1280px-Luttrell_Psalter%2C_A